rleans? Start here. Not only will you get information ..."},{"business_id":"f5xvS-qajT5G84zXF07m8g","review_id":"31PAgIG1izhxbHhJp54QfQ","date":"2015-10-20T01:54:33","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9145947098731995,"text_excerpt":"A great use of a cool old train station building. There's a free small self-guided museum about trains in NOLA. There's a film room where you can see a five minute film on the history of New Orleans. Cute gift shop. Also, a sparkling clean, open to the public, restroom. HURRAY. This space is home base to several tour groups, including Save our Cemeteries."},{"business_id":"f5xvS-qajT5G84zXF07m8g","review_id":"vNlc6jlUg_tSzDgSc8tAbg","date":"2015-09-19T01:32:23","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.912558376789093,"text_excerpt":"I'm a local so the information here is not significantly useful to me, however the Basin St. Station is an excellent location outside the French Quarter. This tourism location is essentially brand new with clean bathrooms and helpful representatives to answer questions for you. There are several brochures of many typical tourist attractions in the city and a gift shop with all the overpriced items you could imagine. This center is very well put together and a great first stop for tourists."}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
